('basilisk','Basilisk','Basilisk','5','Medium','Magical Beast','Always neutral','6d10+12 (45 hp)',45,'–1','20 ft. (4 squares)','16 (–1 Dex, +7 natural), touch 9, flat-footed 16','+6/+8','Bite +8 melee (1d8+3)','5 ft./5 ft.','+9','+4','+3',15,8,15,2,12,11,'Hide +0*, Listen +7, Spot +7','Alertness, Blind-Fight, Great Fortitude','{"special_attacks":"Petrifying gaze","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., low-light vision"}'::jsonb,'A basilisk is a reptilian monster that petrifies living creatures with a mere gaze. A basilisk usually has a dull brown body with a yellowish underbelly. Some specimens sport a short, curved horn atop the nose. An adult basilisk’s body grows to about 6 feet long, not including its tail, which can reach an additional length of 5 to 7 feet. The creature weighs about 300 pounds.','{"full_attack":"Bite +8 melee (1d8+3)","environment":"Warm deserts","organization":"Solitary or colony (3–6)","treasure":"None","advancement":"7–10 HD (Medium); 11–18 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"6d10+12 (45 hp)","hit_points":45,"base_attack_grapple":"+6/+8","attack":"Bite +8 melee (1d8+3)","full_attack":"Bite +8 melee (1d8+3)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +9, Ref +4, Will +3","abilities":{"str":"15","dex":"8","con":"15","int":"2","wis":"12","cha":"11"},"skills":"Hide +0*, Listen +7, Spot +7","feats":"Alertness, Blind-Fight, Great Fortitude","special_attacks":"Petrifying gaze","special_qualities":"Darkvision 60 ft., low-light vision"},"source_file":"monsters-b-c.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-b-c.html',true),
